# Read by ripgrep, and by the search tools of hosts that are built on it, in whatever tree
# holds this skill folder. A project install puts the skill inside the repository being
# worked on (<repository>/.claude/skills/stride-design-review, <repository>/.agents/skills/...),
# and a search of that repository would return lines from it. Measured with the skills then
# installed for two hosts, the portfolio as it then stood: a hidden-aware search for a C
# library function returned 44 skill files against 1 product file.
#
# This hides nothing from a person or from a model that opens a file by its path. It keeps
# the skill's own text out of searches of the code under review:
#   references/   the role files, the protocol, the lenses, the limits
#   scripts/      the tools
#   assets/       the JSON schemas
# SKILL.md stays visible. The patterns are anchored to the skill folder, so a `scripts/` of a
# repository under review is still searched.
# To search the skill itself, ask for it: rg --no-ignore PATTERN <skill folder>.
/references/
/scripts/
/assets/
